The  driver handles resource allocation and device attachment for
the traditional PC/AT keyboard controller. It provides two  logi‐
cal  connections  for  child devices, the slot for a keyboard and
the slot for mice (the latter might be missing in older  keyboard
controllers).  The optional locator argument can be used to force
unusual  connections of devices to logical slots. This feature is
for experimentation only, it will not be useful in normal  opera‐
tion.
